commit 9853dd95cce85eca37ef5fb220b0edce6d8417c7

C03: a file path pasted alone is an unresolved input; the turn names the file and asks what to do with it (FILES1587)

H0299 is a Windows path pasted with no verb («%USERPROFILE%\Desktop\…\ROADMAP.md»); nothing resolved it. `bare_path_file_name` reads a drive, environment-variable or UNC path whose last segment is a file name and names the input kind `bare_path`; `clarify_unresolved_input` composes one short question that names the file by that name only, says the path arrived without a request and asks what to do with the file, and rejects a question that repeats the whole path, claims to have opened or read it, or asks nothing (one corrected retry). The folders stay unsaid: they are the person's. Screened over the whole private registry: only H0299 takes the new kind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


